    {
      "title": "Ratko Mladić, the ‘Butcher of Bosnia’, dies in The Hague",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/ratko-mladic-the-butcher-of-bosnia-dies-aged-84",
      "description": "<p>Bosnian Serb commander responsible for Srebrenica massacre dies in prison while serving life sentence for genocide</p><p>From the archive: </p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/jan/21/14-years-fugitive-hunt-for-ratko-mladic-butcher-of-bosnia\">Fourteen years a fugitive: the hunt for the Butcher of Bosnia </a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/nov/22/ratko-mladic-bosnia-camps-mass-murder-torture-rape-serbian\">Ratko Mladić will die in jail. But go to Bosnia: you’ll see that he won</a></p></li></ul><p>Ratko Mladić, the infamous Serbian general who was serving a life sentence for genocide committed during the Bosnian war, has died in prison in The Hague.</p><p>Mladić had been one of the main architects of the policy of ethnic cleansing during the Bosnian war. He was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/nov/22/ratko-mladic-the-warlike-youth-turned-balkan-war-criminal\">convicted of genocide</a> for orchestrating the 1995 <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/from-the-archive-blog/2020/jul/01/the-srebrenica-massacre-archive-july-1995\">killing of at least 8,000 Muslims in the UN-designated “safe area” Srebrenica</a>, the worst massacre in Europe since the second world war.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/ratko-mladic-the-butcher-of-bosnia-dies-aged-84\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-27T16:12:15"
    },
